cks typecheck+lint+test before completion.\\\"\\n  library-validator:\\n    focus: \\\"Always pass the same spec file used for implementation so quality can validate alignment with specs, not just code quality. Include the spec path, what changed, and what behaviors to validate. Handles testing and quality gates only (documentation moved to library-releaser).\\\"\\n  library-releaser:\\n    focus: \\\"Delegate release tasks: verify quality gates pass, generate documentation (HTML + Markdown), build artifacts, bump version, publish to npm. Provide version bump guidance (patch/minor/major) based on changes since last release. The agent owns the full release lifecycle end-to-end. Docs output: docs/html/ (users) + docs/md/ (agents) at repo root. Agent has docs/** access for writing generated documentation.\\\"\\n\\ndocs_absorbed:\\n  - docs/introduction.md — project vision, file structure, issue properties, CLI overview, config\\n  - docs/hierarchy.md — parent-child tree, childrenOf map, status constraints, auto-promotion\\n  - docs/commands.md — full CLI reference: init, create, update, list, view, history, comments, blockages\\n  - docs/issue-blockages.md — dependency index, blockage lifecycle, cycle detection, impact scoring\\n  - docs/user-auth.md — token-based auth, user registry, auth modes (open/read-only/strict)\\n\\nsession_log:\\n  - session: 1\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-10\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Read all docs, built full understanding of architecture. Could not write expertise files (missing Write/Edit tools). Requested tool update.\\\"\\n  - session: 2\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-10\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Created all 4 expertise files after Write/Edit tools were added. Validated YAML. Expertise fully initialized.\\\"\\n  - session: 3\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-10\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Confirmed expertise is current. No new knowledge gained this session — existing files cover all project docs and architecture.\\\"\\n  - session: 4\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-10\\\"\\n    