summary: \\\"Picked up docs task mpfm9qxpsd via /agentrack-implement. Blockage from implementation mpfm9aff8v was resolved. Read all 4 target docs files and the spec. Attempted to update cli-reference.md but hit access restriction — CTO has read-only access to docs/markdown/, only library-releaser has write access. Reassigned mpfm9qxpsd to library-releaser with comment explaining the interface is stable (bugs in mpfn4dkotn are runtime-only, spec/CLI interface unchanged). Key lesson: CTO cannot update docs directly — always delegate docs tasks to library-releaser.\\\"\\n  - session: 74\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-21\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Planned E2E test refactor via /issue skill. Spec already existed at .agentic/specs/e2e-refactor.md (authored by library-validator). Prerequisite (--branch flag) already implemented. Skipped spec draft and review phases — implementer wrote the spec themselves. Created issue chain: parent mpfobnq8ty (CTO, in-progress, child of mpebmstgs9), implementation mpfobxibgb (library-validator), validation mpfoc9r65a (library-validator, blocked by impl). No library-developer or library-releaser involvement — pure test refactoring task.\\\"\\n  - session: 75\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-22\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Launched webapp initiative. User requested a web UI for managing agentrack issues. Read all agentrack docs (8 files) to understand full API surface. Created 3 deliverables: (1) Comprehensive spec (.agentic/specs/webapp-spec.md, 24KB) — REST API design (21 endpoints across issues/comments/blockages/users/sync/health), frontend design (React+Vite+shadcn/ui, 2-page SPA with list+detail), backend design (Hono+Bun, thin REST layer over agentrack JS API), frontend architecture (TanStack Query, React Router, component tree). (2) Phased roadmap (.agentic/specs/webapp-roadmap.md) — 5 phases with validation criteria: Foundation → Core issues → Rich detail → Users & sync → Polish. (3) 10 implementation issues with blocking dependencies. Registered webapp-developer and webapp-validator in agentrack (tokens tk_thd0nvbd, tk_f1g3kazq). Created agent setup guide (.agentic/specs/webapp-agent-setup.md) since CTO lacks write access to .claude/agents/ and .agentic/expertise/ for other agents. Updated CTO expertise with new subordinates.\\\"\\n  - session: 76\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-27\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Picked up mpo1tdrjdm (mentions feature) via /agentrack-implement. Spec already existed at .agentic/specs/mentions-spec.md. Found pre-existing duplicate chain (mpo1to0veg/tpihee/u7xkl4/urfo4z/uzzj86) with completed reviews. Both reviews had detailed feedback: dev review found auth model mismatch (requiresIdentity flag needed), worktree init path, rebuild-with-revoked-users, case normalization issues. Quality review found regex edge case (double @), atomicity wording, missing NOT_INITIALIZED errors, update-resets-isRead behavior, mentionsList auth asymmetry. Updated spec to REVIEWED with 6 clarifications: improved regex (/(?:^|(?<=[^@\\\\w]))@([\\\\w-]+)/g), requiresIdentity flag for auth, NOT_INITIALIZED on all methods, rebuild extracts all @names, case normalization, honest atomicity wording. Closed old duplicate chain. Created new chain: mpo1wn9vsi (impl, unblocked) → mpo1wwsikr (validation, blocked by impl) → mpo1x35lft (docs+build, blocked by validation). Parent stays in-progress awaiting runner.\\\"\\n  - session: 77\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-27\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Planned removal of issueTitle from mention list response. Focused API refinement — issueTitle is unnecessary coupling (consumers can look up the issue themselves). Skipped spec and reviews (obvious fix, well-scoped). Created issue chain: parent mpo5brxipq (CTO, in-progress), implement mpo5c0hty7 (library-developer, unblocked), validate mpo5c8otiz (library-validator, blocked by impl). Initially forgot docs+build task.\\\"\\n  - session: 78\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-27\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"User flagged that mentions docs weren't updated after the mentions feature work. Created retroactive docs+build task mpo6vnff2i (library-releaser, todo) under mpo5brxipq. Covers both: (1) mentions feature documentation (cli-reference.md, javascript-reference.md) and (2) issueTitle removal from docs. Lesson reinforced: EVERY issue chain that touches CLI/API MUST include a library-releaser task — no exceptions, even for 'small' refinements.\\\"\\n  - session: 79\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-27\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Handled /work-mention mpoe57bo11 — mention was just 'Hey @cto ' with no specific request on mpgquqm43b (webapp Phase 4a). Incomplete/accidental mention, no action needed. Marked as read. Updated expertise: closed both parent issues mpo1tdrjdm (mentions feature) and mpo5brxipq (issueTitle removal) — all children were done. Noted stale old issues (configurable branch mpfn4dkotn, E2E refactor mpfobnq8ty) no longer in index — likely from different worktree branch. Discovered duplicate mentions chain mpmvdvi6lr (also all done).\\\"\\n  - session: 80\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-28\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Planned webapp initiative from tmp/webapp.md. Existing specs (webapp-spec.md, webapp-roadmap.md) already aligned with requirements. Created 11 issues in agentrack: parent mppqqp8y26 (in-progress, CTO), 5 implementation tasks for webapp-developer, 5 validation tasks for webapp-validator. Sequential dependency chain: Phase 1 impl → Phase 1 validate → Phase 2 impl → ... → Phase 5 validate. Each implementation task has detailed scope comment referencing the spec and roadmap. Initially left all issues in idea status — agent runner couldn't pick them up. Moved Phase 1 (mppqqte6gs) to todo, confirmed via agt next. Key lesson: agent runner only picks up todo status, not idea.\\\"\\n  - session: 81\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-29\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Planned isolated E2E data fix as TOP PRIORITY. Problem: webapp-validator's 114+ Playwright tests pollute main .agentrack/ with test issues (no delete API — recently cleaned up 416 manually). Solution: use validation/.e2edata/ isolated worktree via AGENTRACK_CWD env var (rename from typo AGENTACK_CWD). Spec at .agentic/tmp/isolated-web-validation.md. Created issue chain under mppqqp8y26: parent mpqn5bi2us (CTO, in-progress, P1), impl mpqn5i7wui (webapp-developer, todo), validation mpqn5qf6zq (webapp-validator, blocked by impl). Blocked Phase 4 validation (mppqt90kot) on isolation validation — prevents further pollution before fix ships. Phase 4 impl (mppqswn3jl) still in-progress with webapp-developer in parallel.\\\"\\n  - session: 83\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-29\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Diagnosed why no agents were working. Root cause: mppqswn3jl (Phase 4 impl) was stuck in-progress — webapp-developer set it to in-progress at 07:17 but session ended without writing any Phase 4 code. Since agt next only returns todo issues, agent runner couldn't pick it up. Also found mpqn5bi2us (E2E isolation parent) still in-progress despite both children done. Fixes applied: closed mpqn5bi2us (done), reset mppqswn3jl back to todo. Board now clean: 3 done, 3 open (mppqqp8y26 in-progress, mppqswn3jl todo, mppqt90kot todo+blocked). New lesson: orphaned in-progress issues block the entire agent runner — always check for them when agents aren't picking up work.\\\"\\n  - session: 84\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-29\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Diagnosed E2E isolation breach — reuseExistingServer:true defeats AGENTRACK_CWD. Created two fix issues: mpr50trdgw (webapp-developer, dedicated test ports 3001/5174, reuseExistingServer false, vite env var config, test URL updates) and mpr51myb9q (webapp-validator, verify no pollution in main .agentrack/). Blocked mppqt90kot (Phase 4 validation) on mpr50trdgw. Hit blocker: cto wasn't registered in agentrack — enforce-agentrack-token hook denied all agt commands. User registered cto. Initially created issues in idea status — user flagged nobody picks them up. Fixed by updating both to todo. Key lessons: (1) reuseExistingServer:true is a test isolation anti-pattern when env vars control server behavior, (2) cto needs to be registered in agentrack users for agt CLI access, (3) agt create defaults to idea status — MUST agt update to todo immediately after creation, (4) the hook reads users.json BEFORE the bash command runs so self-registration in same call doesn't work.\\\"\\n  - session: 85\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-29\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Onboarded new subordinate webapp-styler (UI/UX expert). Created two issues under webapp epic (mppqqp8y26): (1) mpr7q3putx — UI/UX audit task for webapp-styler (todo, P2) to explore webapp frontend and produce prioritized findings comment (critical/high/medium/low), explicitly read-only no code changes. (2) mpr7qd6bjq — CTO review task (todo, P2, blocked by mpr7q3putx) to process the audit, evaluate findings, cluster into batches, and create implementation issues for webapp-styler. Updated expertise: added webapp-styler to subordinates list, refreshed expertise_status with new issues.\\\"\\n  - session: 86\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-29\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Completed CTO review of UI/UX audit (mpr7qd6bjq). Evaluated webapp-styler's audit findings and created 6 implementation issues in dependency order: (1) mpraw5x3rp — design tokens + CSS variable system (P1, foundation, unblocked), (2) mprawicnef — status badges + priority indicators (P2, blocked by 1), (3) mprawwui44 — loading states + empty states (P2, blocked by 1), (4) mpraxha5es — form UX + accessibility (P2, blocked by 1), (5) mpray2w1kj — layout + navigation + responsiveness (P2, blocked by 1), (6) mpraygczia — micro-interactions + polish (P3, blocked by 1-5, final pass). Design tokens (1) must ship first — all other issues consume the CSS variables. Issues 2-5 can run in parallel once tokens are done. Issue 6 is the final polish pass that refines the output of 2-5.\\\"\\n  - session: 87\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-30\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"User requested complete deletion (not just closure) of all webapp-styler issues from agentrack. Deleted 8 issue files (mpraw5x3rp, mprawicnef, mprawwui44, mpraxha5es, mpray2w1kj, mpraygczia, mpr7q3putx, mpr7qd6bjq) and cleaned index.json (open/closed/childrenOf) and dependencies.json references. agt CLI has no delete command — used node scripts to directly manipulate the file-backed store. Key learning: index.json structure is {open:[], closed:[], childrenOf:{}}, not {issues:[]}. webapp-styler remains an active subordinate.\\\"\\n  - session: 88\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-30\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Planned agt delete command feature. User realized there's no way to delete issues from agentrack — had to manually manipulate files in session 87. Investigated full codebase: types, tracker, index-manager, dependency-manager, mentions, events, CLI runner, existing e2e test patterns. Wrote comprehensive spec (.agentic/specs/delete-command-spec.md): hard delete with cascade, bidirectional blockage cleanup, mentions cleanup, parent-child relationship cleanup, event file removal. Created 3-issue chain: mps4sfny0f (impl, library-developer) → mps4uwcsqx (validation, library-validator, blocked by impl) → mps4viae0a (docs, library-releaser, blocked by validation). Validation and docs are children of impl. Updated expertise.\\\"\\n  - session: 89\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-30\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Agents weren't picking up issues. Diagnosed: mps4sfny0f was stuck in-progress assigned to cto (not library-developer), and it was parent of validation/docs — hierarchy constraint prevented closing parent with non-done children. Detached children from parent, marked impl done. Also reset mppqswn3jl (stuck in-progress) back to todo. User asked about JS library readiness for delete — confirmed issueDelete is implemented and types exported but javascript-reference.md was missing docs entirely. Reopened mps4viae0a (was marked done) with detailed gap description. JS reference subsequently updated by library-releaser with full issueDelete method section + exported types. Closed mps4viae0a. Delete command feature now fully complete (impl + validation + bug fix + docs). Key lesson: parent-child hierarchy on issue chains creates a catch-22 with done constraints — prefer flat sibling chains with blockages instead.\\\"\\n  - session: 89\\n    date: \\\"2026-05-30\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Picked up bug mpscu5l9rk (removeAllBlockagesForIssue inverted counterpart filter). Found during delete command validation (mps4uwcsqx). One-line fix: filter uses issueId instead of entry.blockerId when cleaning counterpart entries from blocks map. CTO can't edit source files — delegated to library-developer via child issue mpscw71ria (todo, unblocked). Blockage chain: mpscw71ria → mpscu5l9rk → mps4uwcsqx (delete validation). Parent stays in-progress until child completes.\\\"\\n  - session: 90\\n    date: \\\"2026-06-01\\\"\\n    summary: \\\"Stop hook triggered expertise update. Board audit: 13 issues (10 done, 2 in-progress, 1 todo). Fixed stale counts in expertise_status (was '7 done', now '10 done'). Fixed project_overview stage — removed 'E2E isolation BROKEN' (now fixed), added 'Delete command shipped', updated Phase 4 description. No new work.\\\"\\n\"}}","stderr":"","exitCode":0,"command":"bun .claude/skills/agent-expertise/expertise.hook.ts","durationMs":33},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5d850713-ea5d-4a8c-9fe2-b8005dec81f8","timestamp":"2026-06-01T17:43:18.457Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/Users/javi/projects/agentrack","sessionId":"27152081-2b2a-4a32-8c49-5eb5356fd1c4","version":"2.1.159","gitBranch":"main"}
