{"parentUuid":"f85d4fb2-773e-4311-b3fe-b9972f8886ea","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"156a6783-2847-4e1a-b65e-8e2be4c7e0ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"tool_result","content":"agent 'cto' may not access path outside project: /Users/javi/.claude/projects/-Users-javi-projects-agentrack/27152081-2b2a-4a32-8c49-5eb5356fd1c4/tool-results/hook-052239d3-acb6-48e5-b3b3-0fd45fceb2f2-1-additionalContext.txt","is_error":true,"tool_use_id":"call_e1bb47c54790421bba01fa0a"}]},"uuid":"44b72177-fe1d-41fc-8659-3be39f3ddd25","timestamp":"2026-06-01T17:43:32.221Z","toolUseResult":"Error: agent 'cto' may not access path outside project: /Users/javi/.claude/projects/-Users-javi-projects-agentrack/27152081-2b2a-4a32-8c49-5eb5356fd1c4/tool-results/hook-052239d3-acb6-48e5-b3b3-0fd45fceb2f2-1-additionalContext.txt","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"f85d4fb2-773e-4311-b3fe-b9972f8886ea","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/Users/javi/projects/agentrack","sessionId":"27152081-2b2a-4a32-8c49-5eb5356fd1c4","version":"2.1.159","gitBranch":"main"}
appended: {"parentUuid":"165f0ae3-9bdf-4275-aefd-097af007e412","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"156a6783-2847-4e1a-b65e-8e2be4c7e0ec","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"call_573ba0a8144e4bfb8ee7caca","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# CTO Expertise Index\n2\t# Agent: cto\n3\t# Domain: Project architecture, technical specifications, development alignment\n4\t\n5\thierarchy:\n6\t  manager: none — top-level agent\n7\t  subordinates:\n8\t    active:\n9\t      - library-developer (implementation)\n10\t      - library-validator (testing, quality gates — documentation removed)\n11\t      - library-releaser (release prep, documentation, build, version management, publishing)\n12\t      - webapp-developer (full-stack web development — React frontend + Hono backend)\n13\t      - webapp-validator (webapp testing, quality assurance, spec compliance)\n14\t      - webapp-styler (UI/UX expert — visual design, interaction patterns, accessibility, polish)\n15\t    pending_setup: []\n16\t\n17\texpertise_status: \"Webapp initiative (parent mppqqp8y26, in-progress). Phases 1-3 done. Phase 4 impl (mppqswn3jl) in-progress with webapp-developer. Phase 4 validation (mppqt90kot) todo, blocked by mppqswn3jl. E2E isolation FIXED: mpr50trdgw + mpr51myb9q both DONE. Delete command FULLY COMPLETE: impl (mps4sfny0f) done, validation (mps4uwcsqx) done, bug fix (mpscu5l9rk+mpscw71ria) done, docs (mps4viae0a) done — both cli-reference.md and javascript-reference.md updated. Board: 13 issues (10 done, 2 in-progress, 1 todo). webapp-styler active but no assigned issues.\"\n18\t\n19\tproject_overview:\n20\t  name: agentrack\n21\t  previous_name: trackgentic (renamed 2026-05-18)\n22\t  type: npm library (TypeScript, Bun runtime)\n23\t  purpose: Issue tracker designed for AI agents — file-backed, event-sourced, git-friendly\n24\t  distribution: npm package with CLI entry point (`agt` command)\n25\t  stage: \"Dogfooding active. All 7 library phases complete + build pipeline. Delete command shipped. Mentions feature shipped. Webapp initiative active (parent mppqqp8y26, in-progress): Phases 1-3 done, Phase 4 (users & sync) in-progress with webapp-developer (mppqswn3jl). E2E isolation fixed (dedicated test ports). Public docs at docs/markdown/ (8 files).\"\n26\t  bun_version: \"1.3.11\"\n27\t  build_tool: tsup (implemented, producing dist/)\n28\t  docs_tool: \"Hand-written markdown docs in docs/markdown/ (8 sections). TypeDoc removed. Docs overhaul in progress (mpdpt4rego), validation pending (mpdpv6gw49). Future: Docusaurus site consuming docs/markdown/ (mpdxdbqwt9, idea). Spec: .agentic/specs/user-docs-spec.md.\"\n29\t\n30\tdetail_files:\n31\t  - path: architecture.yaml\n32\t    description: Core data model, file structure, event sourcing, resolution algorithm, index design\n33\t  - path: design-decisions.yaml\n34\t    description: Architectural decisions and rationale (why file-backed, why event-sourced, etc.)\n35\t  - path: status.yaml\n36\t    description: Current project status, implementation roadmap, open questions, risks\n37\t\n38\tspecifications:\n39\t  location: .agentic/specs/\n40\t  files:\n41\t    - path: 01-overview.md\n42\t      description: Monorepo structure, library package layout, design principles, dependencies, CLI/API relationship\n43\t    - path: 02-data-model.md\n44\t      description: All TypeScript types, interfaces, file formats, initial file contents\n45\t    - path: 03-api-specification.md\n46\t      description: Every Tracker method with params, return types, behavior, error handling\n47\t    - path: 04-cli-specification.md\n48\t      description: Every CLI command with args, flags, auth, output format, error handling\n49\t    - path: 05-implementation-phases.md\n50\t      description: 7 phases from foundation to polish, with tasks, tests, and exit criteria per phase\n51\t    - path: 06-quality-plan.md\n52\t      description: Quality plan — now uses Prettier + ESLint (was Biome). Linting, typechecking (strict+), testing (Bun), test organization, documentation (TypeDoc), quality gates\n53\t    - path: 07-phase3-auth-users.md\n54\t      description: Phase 3 specification — auth module (resolveAuthor), user CRUD (register/list/revoke/regenerate), auth integration into existing methods, CLI user commands\n55\t    - path: 07-phase4-comments-spec.md\n56\t      description: Phase 4 specification — computeComments function, 4 Tracker comment methods, CLI comment commands, test plan\n57\t    - path: 08-phase5-hierarchy-spec.md\n58\t      description: Phase 5 specification — childrenOf map management, hierarchy.ts (upward/downward constraints), Tracker create/update integration, reparenting, test plan\n59\t    - path: 07-phase6-blockages-spec.md\n60\t      description: Phase 6 specification — dependency-manager (bidirectional maps, cycle detection, batch atomicity, impact score), 4 Tracker blockage methods, auto-resolution on status change, CLI blockage commands, test plan\n61\t    - path: 08-phase7-polish-spec.md\n62\t      description: Phase 7 specification — JSDoc on all public API, error message polish, edge case & resilience testing, package configuration verification\n63\t    - path: next-command-spec.md\n64\t      description: \"`next <user-name>` command — recommend highest-priority unblocked issue for a user. Returns ComputedIssue or NO_ISSUES_AVAILABLE. Filters by assignee, actionable statuses (idea/todo/in-progress), no active blockages. Sort: priority ASC → impact DESC → id ASC.\"\n65\t    - path: next-todo-only-spec.md\n66\t      description: \"Amends next-command-spec: restrict status filter from [idea, todo, in-progress] to [todo] only. Single-line change in Tracker.next(). REVIEWED — reviews skipped (trivially scoped). Implementation mp9zda04cp in-progress with library-developer.\"\n67\t    - path: cap-upward-promotion-spec.md\n68\t      description: \"Cap upward auto-promotion at in-progress. Parents never auto-promote to done/closed via computeUpwardPromotions. Spec status: REVIEWED. Reason format: auto-promoted to TARGET: child advanced to CHILD. 7 new test cases required.\"\n69\t    - path: independent-git-spec.md\n70\t      description: \"Store .agentrack/ on orphan branch _agentrack via git worktree. Branch-independent issue access. Two init scenarios (fresh/join). Three commands: agt init (worktree setup), agt push (auto-commit + sync), agt pull (sync from remote). New module src/worktree.ts + 2 new CLI commands. Status: IMPLEMENTED with 3 spec deviations found in validation. Fix phase: mpd4hktoxq (fix deviations) → mpd4hs14zp (validate + tests) → mpd4i06wz6 (document + build). Parent: mpcwcufhzk.\"\n71\t      naming_conventions: \"Branch = `_agentrack`, directory = `.agentrack`, tool = `agentrack`, data inside branch = `issues/`\"\n72\t    - path: docs-generation.md\n73\t      description: \"SUPERSEDED by user-docs-spec.md. TypeDoc dual-format docs are being removed. Release workflow and .gitignore updated by CTO (mpdpvfn3yb done). Typedoc tooling cleanup pending (mpdpu00ksc).\"\n74\t    - path: user-docs-spec.md\n75\t      description: \"User-friendly documentation overhaul. Replace TypeDoc auto-generated docs with hand-written markdown in docs/markdown/. 8 sections: overview, getting started, authentication, issue object, hierarchy & blockages, storing in git, CLI reference, JS reference. Removes typedoc tooling entirely. Parent: mpdpt4rego. CTO config (mpdpvfn3yb) done. TypeDoc deps removed from package.json. Doc writing: mpdwq7dvls (library-releaser, replaces failed mpdpuhd0r5).\"\n76\t    - path: configurable-branch-spec.md\n77\t      description: \"Configurable branch name for agt init. --branch <name> flag allows custom orphan branch per agentrack instance. Normalization: strip leading _, prepend _ for branch, . for dir. Pointer file (.agentrack.json) at repo root solves circular discovery. Slash rejection (AC8). resolution.ts and tracker.ts dynamic discovery via pointer file. New module: src/core/pointer.ts (actually implemented as branch-config.ts). Enables multiple instances per repo and test isolation. IMPLEMENTED (mpfm9aff8v) but validation (mpfm9ixr9i) found 2 critical bugs: (1) double directory creation — tracker init runs before branch flag takes effect, leaving stale .agentrack/ alongside custom dir, (2) missing BRANCH_CONFLICT detection. Fix: mpfn4dkotn (library-developer). Parent: mpfm8bilwf. Spec status: REVIEWED.\"\n78\t    - path: e2e-validation-suite-spec.md\n79\t      description: \"E2E test suite in validation/ folder. Uses real git repos + agt CLI invocations (spawn + capture). Covers all CLI commands with happy/error/edge cases. Full lifecycle test. No library code changes. Parent: mpebmstgs9. Implementation: mpebnnq5qq (library-validator).\"\n80\t    - path: e2e-refactor.md\n81\t      description: \"Refactor E2E tests from per-test git repos to shared worktree approach. Two test types: Type A (git ops: init/push/pull, clean git env per test) and Type B (CRUD etc., fast data reset per test). New helpers: initE2EWorktree, teardownE2EWorktree, resetWorktreeData, setAuthMode. Remove old helpers: createTestRepo, cleanupTestRepo, createIsolatedDir. Parent: mpfobnq8ty (child of mpebmstgs9). Implementation: mpfobxibgb (library-validator). Validation: mpfoc9r65a (library-validator).\"\n82\t    - path: webapp-spec.md\n83\t      description: \"Full-stack webapp specification for agentrack UI. React 19 + Vite + shadcn/ui frontend (SPA with list and detail views), Hono + Bun backend (REST API with 21 endpoints), TanStack Query state management. Covers API design (issues, comments, blockages, users, sync, health), UI/UX design (tree view, filters, inline editing, responsive layout), project structure, color scheme. v1 scope excludes init, custom branches, auth UI, real-time, markdown rendering, dark mode.\"\n84\t    - path: webapp-roadmap.md\n85\t      description: \"5-phase development roadmap for the webapp. Phase 1: Foundation (scaffolding, health check). Phase 2: Core issues (CRUD endpoints, list page, detail page, create dialog). Phase 3: Rich detail (comments, blockages, history, tree view, tags, parent). Phase 4: Users & sync (user management UI, push/pull controls). Phase 5: Polish (responsive, loading states, sorting, filtering). 10 implementation issues with blocking dependencies.\"\n86\t    - path: webapp-agent-setup.md\n87\t      description: \"Setup guide for webapp-developer and webapp-validator agents. Contains full agent configurations (frontmatter + system prompts) and expertise index templates. Agents registered in agentrack but need manual file creation in .claude/agents/ and .agentic/expertise/.\"\n88\t    - path: delete-command-spec.md\n89\t      description: \"Spec for agt delete <issue-id> command. Hard delete of issue and all descendants. Cleans blockages (bidirectional), mentions, parent-child relationships, and event file from disk. Returns deletedIds array (children first, target last). New types: IssueDeleteParams, IssueDeleteResult. New helpers: removeIssueMentions, removeAllBlockagesForIssue. Parent: mps4sfny0f.\"\n90\t\n91\taccess_boundaries:\n92\t  rule: \"CTO must NOT read or modify files under packages/library/. All code changes go through subordinates.\"\n93\t  cto_scope: \".agentic/ files, root-level config, specifications, expertise files\"\n94\t  code_access: \"If code-level insight is needed, ask library-developer or library-validator to report — never read source directly.\"\n95\t  enforced: \"2026-05-10 — user explicitly removed CTO read permissions on packages/library/\"\n96\t\n97\tdelegation_workflow:\n98\t  mandatory_sequence: |\n99\t    After every library-developer delegation that makes code changes, you MUST delegate to library-validator for validation.\n100\t    Sequence: library-developer (implement) → library-validator (validate).\n101\t    Never skip the quality validation step. This ensures code is clean, tested, and documented.\n102\t  timeout_constraint: |\n103\t    Bash tool has a 10-minute (600000ms) timeout. Large phases must be split into sub-delegations of ~5-8 minutes each.\n104\t    Split strategy for Phase 3: (A) auth.ts + errors.ts, (B) user methods in tracker.ts, (C) auth integration into existing methods + CLI commands, (D) library-validator validation).\n105\t    Each sub-task should be scoped to a few files to stay within timeout.\n106\t  docs_ownership: |\n107\t    library-releaser owns documentation tasks: TypeDoc configuration, doc generation, docs scripts.\n108\t    When docs need updating or generating for a release, delegate to library-releaser.\n109\t    library-validator no longer handles documentation — only testing and quality gates.\n110\t  api_change_policy: |\n111\t    MANDATORY: Any change to CLI command behavior or to the API of public functions must be\n112\t    delegated to library-releaser for running the build and updating documentation.\n113\t    This applies to ALL code changes that touch public-facing surface area — whether new features,\n114\t    behavioral changes, or signature modifications. library-releaser must rebuild dist/ and update\n115\t    docs/markdown/ to reflect the change before the work is considered complete.\n116\t    ENFORCEMENT: Every /issue chain that touches CLI or public API MUST include a library-releaser\n117\t    task as part of the issue chain. Do NOT mark the parent as done until library-releaser completes.\n118\t    Violation caught in session 68: configurable-branch shipped without docs+build task.\n119\t  docs_awareness: |\n120\t    All agents have read access to docs/markdown/ (8 files: overview, getting-started, authentication,\n121\t    issue-object, hierarchy-and-blockages, storing-issues-in-git, cli-reference, javascript-reference).\n122\t    Agents can consult these docs for API details, CLI usage patterns, and feature behavior.\n123\t    library-releaser has docs_structure in its expertise file with full file listing.\n124\t    When delegating tasks, mention docs/ availability if the agent might benefit from reference material.\n125\t  access_gaps: |\n126\t    Resolved: user granted CTO access to .github/ folder. CTO now owns workflow files.\n127\t    Root .gitignore is also writable by CTO.\n128\t  validation_rejection_flow: |\n129\t    When a validator rejects an implementation (reports issues):\n130\t    1. Validator posts a comment on their issue with findings and keeps it in their status (or reopens)\n131\t    2. CTO reviews the findings and reopens the implementation issue (move back to todo/in-progress)\n132\t    3. Developer picks up the reopened issue, makes fixes, marks done again\n133\t    4. Validator re-validates — cycle continues until implementation passes\n134\t    This is the same pattern used for library issues (e.g., configurable branch mpfn4dkotn fix cycle).\n135\t  webapp_delegation_pattern: |\n136\t    Webapp issues follow sequential phases: impl → validate → next phase impl.\n137\t    ALL issues in a chain should be set to todo upfront. Blockages control the execution order.\n138\t    Only todo issues are picked up by `agt next`. Idea is invisible to the runner.\n139\t    Do NOT use idea status for work that should flow through the agent runner automatically.\n140\t  webapp_styler_pattern: |\n141\t    webapp-styler is a UI/UX specialist — does NOT write backend code or tests.\n142\t    Workflow: (1) webapp-styler audits UI and posts findings comment, (2) CTO reviews findings\n143\t    and creates implementation issues, (3) webapp-styler implements changes within scope.\n144\t    webapp-styler's domain: CSS, component styling, layout, accessibility, responsive design,\n145\t    interaction patterns, visual consistency, micro-interactions.\n146\t    webapp-styler does NOT own: backend API, data model, business logic, test infrastructure.\n147\t    Currently no assigned issues — cleared in session 87. Ready for new tasks when needed.\n148\t  note: \"Self-check and validation steps are enforced via agent system prompts. No need to duplicate in delegation messages.\"\n149\t  library-developer:\n150\t    focus: \"Focus delegation messages on the implementation task itself. The agent self-checks typecheck+lint+test before completion.\"\n151\t  library-validator:\n152\t    focus: \"Always pass the same spec file used for implementation so quality can validate alignment with specs, not just code quality. Include the spec path, what changed, and what behaviors to validate. Handles testing and quality gates only (documentation moved to library-releaser).\"\n153\t  library-releaser:\n154\t    focus: \"Delegate release tasks: verify quality gates pass, generate documentation (HTML + Markdown), build artifacts, bump version, publish to npm. Provide version bump guidance (patch/minor/major) based on changes since last release. The agent owns the full release lifecycle end-to-end. Docs output: docs/html/ (users) + docs/md/ (agents) at repo root. Agent has docs/** access for writing generated documentation.\"\n155\t\n156\tdocs_absorbed:\n157\t  - docs/introduction.md — project vision, file structure, issue properties, CLI overview, config\n158\t  - docs/hierarchy.md — parent-child tree, childrenOf map, status constraints, auto-promotion\n159\t  - docs/commands.md — full CLI reference: init, create, update, list, view, history, comments, blockages\n160\t  - docs/issue-blockages.md — dependency index, blockage lifecycle, cycle detection, impact scoring\n161\t  - docs/user-auth.md — token-based auth, user registry, auth modes (open/read-only/strict)\n162\t\n163\tsession_log:\n164\t  - session: 1\n165\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n166\t    summary: \"Read all docs, built full understanding of architecture. Could not write expertise files (missing Write/Edit tools). Requested tool update.\"\n167\t  - session: 2\n168\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n169\t    summary: \"Created all 4 expertise files after Write/Edit tools were added. Validated YAML. Expertise fully initialized.\"\n170\t  - session: 3\n171\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n172\t    summary: \"Confirmed expertise is current. No new knowledge gained this session — existing files cover all project docs and architecture.\"\n173\t  - session: 4\n174\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n175\t    summary: \"Generated full library specifications (5 files in .agentic/specs/). Resolved OQ-001 (specs location) and OQ-002 (programmatic API). Updated expertise and status. Ready to delegate to library-developer.\"\n176\t  - session: 5\n177\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n178\t    summary: \"User requested monorepo creation. Attempted to create root package.json and packages/library/ files but hit read-only access restriction. CTO agent can write .agentic/ files but not repo source files. Awaiting permission update or alternative approach.\"\n179\t  - session: 6\n180\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n181\t    summary: \"User updated permissions. Root-level ./* write works. Discovered packages/** subdirectory is not covered — Bash mkdir and file writes to packages/library/ are blocked. Identified needed access rule: 'packages/** with read+write'. Awaiting user to add it.\"\n182\t  - session: 7\n183\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n184\t    summary: \"User created packages/library/ folder. Attempted monorepo initialization but still blocked — ./* access rule only covers root-level files, not packages/** subdirectories. Requested user add 'packages/** with [read, write]' access rule.\"\n185\t  - session: 8\n186\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n187\t    summary: \"User granted packages/** access. Initialized monorepo: root package.json, packages/library/ with package.json/tsconfig.json/bunfig.toml, full src/ and tests/ directory tree. Initially overstepped by writing type source files — user corrected to scaffold only. Deleted all source files, kept config only. Ran bun install successfully.\"\n188\t  - session: 9\n189\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n190\t    summary: \"User hired library-developer subordinate. CTO permissions removed from packages/library. Delegated Phase 1 (Foundation) to library-developer. Phase 1 completed successfully: all types, core modules (errors, id, resolution, file-io, tracker.init), CLI runner with init command, barrel exports. 18 tests, 432 assertions, typecheck clean. Ready for Phase 2.\"\n191\t  - session: 10\n192\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n193\t    summary: \"User hired library-validator subordinate. Created quality plan specification (06-quality-plan.md): Biome for linting, strict TypeScript with extra flags, Bun test runner with coverage thresholds, test file organization (core/cli/integration/helpers), code review checklist, TypeDoc for documentation with typedoc-plugin-markdown. Defined documentation update process triggered by code changes. Updated expertise index with new subordinate.\"\n194\t  - session: 11\n195\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n196\t    summary: \"Onboarded library-validator. Delegated quality plan implementation: install Biome/TypeDoc, create biome.json/typedoc.json configs, update bunfig.toml for coverage, add strict TS flags (noUncheckedIndexedAccess, exactOptionalPropertyTypes, etc.), restructure test dirs (cli/commands/, integration/, helpers/), run all quality gates. Task running in background, awaiting results.\"\n197\t  - session: 12\n198\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n199\t    summary: \"library-validator completed quality plan implementation. All gates pass: typecheck (zero errors with 4 extra strict flags), lint (zero errors after Biome auto-fixes for import ordering, template literals, null checks), tests (18 pass, 433 assertions, 88.91% coverage), docs:check (TypeDoc parses cleanly). Verified with bun run quality. Ready for Phase 2.\"\n200\t  - session: 13\n201\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n202\t    summary: \"Designed agent handoff workflow. Proposed: library-developer runs typecheck+lint before completing tasks (self-check), library-validator runs full quality gate + generates missing tests. Recommended creating 07-workflow.md spec, adding delegation template to CTO expertise, and updating agent system prompts with mandatory pre-completion steps. User asked to also update CTO expertise with this knowledge.\"\n203\t  - session: 14\n204\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n205\t    summary: \"User confirmed they updated agent system prompts (library-developer.md and library-validator.md) with mandatory pre-completion steps. All three layers of the handoff workflow are now in place: (1) agent system prompts with mandatory self-checks, (2) CTO delegation templates in expertise, (3) user-confirmed prompt changes. Ready to proceed with Phase 2 delegation.\"\n206\t  - session: 15\n207\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n208\t    summary: \"User clarified: self-check steps are now in agent system prompts, so no need to duplicate them in delegation messages. Simplified delegation_templates to a note that system prompts handle enforcement, with focus on task content only. Updated expertise_status accordingly.\"\n209\t  - session: 16\n210\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n211\t    summary: \"User emphasized: always delegate to library-validator after every library-developer code change. Added mandatory_sequence to delegation_workflow in expertise: developer (implement) → quality (validate). Never skip the quality step. Renamed delegation_templates to delegation_workflow for clarity.\"\n212\t  - session: 17\n213\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n214\t    summary: \"Delegated Phase 2 (Event Engine & CRUD) to library-developer. Implementation completed: event engine (appendEvent, replayEvents, computeState), index manager (binary search, immutable operations), Tracker CRUD (create, list, view, update, history), 5 CLI commands. Developer hit strict TS + Biome tension (noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature vs UseLiteralKeys, cognitive complexity). Resolved by refactoring. Delegated to library-validator for validation: all gates pass, 122 tests, 742 assertions, 99.11% coverage (100% functions). Quality added 19 new tests covering gaps (file-io error paths, index-manager edge cases, tracker error codes). Phase 2 complete.\"\n215\t  - session: 18\n216\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n217\t    summary: \"User asked about Biome vs tsc value. Explained complementary roles: tsc catches type errors, Biome catches code quality issues (unused vars, cognitive complexity, formatting). Documented the TS/Biome tension pattern (noPropertyAccessFromIndexSignature vs UseLiteralKeys) and resolution (typed interfaces over Record). Added DD-014 (Biome for linting alongside strict TypeScript) to design-decisions.yaml.\"\n218\t  - session: 19\n219\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n220\t    summary: \"User enforced strict access boundaries: CTO can no longer read packages/library/. All code interaction must flow through subordinates (library-developer for implementation, library-validator for validation). Updated expertise with access_boundaries section. Ready to delegate Phase 3 (Auth & Users).\"\n221\t  - session: 20\n222\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n223\t    summary: \"Created Phase 3 spec (07-phase3-auth-users.md) covering auth module, user CRUD, auth integration into existing methods, CLI user commands. Attempted to delegate full Phase 3 to library-developer but hit 10-minute Bash tool timeout — task too large for single delegation. Identified need to split Phase 3 into smaller sub-delegations (~5-8 min each). Updated expertise with timeout_constraint in delegation_workflow. Next: split Phase 3 into sub-tasks (A: auth.ts + errors, B: user methods, C: auth integration + CLI).\"\n224\t  - session: 21\n225\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n226\t    summary: \"User reported library-developer finished Phase 3 coding but Biome was blocking. Decision: replace Biome with Prettier + ESLint for faster development. Updated DD-014 in design-decisions.yaml. Delegated tooling swap to library-developer (remove biome.json, add .prettierrc + eslint.config.js, update scripts). Completed successfully. Delegated to library-validator for validation: all gates pass, 45 new tests added (13 auth unit tests, 23 user+auth integration tests, 9 CLI user command tests). Phase 3 complete: 167 tests, 846 assertions, 99.22% coverage. Tooling: Prettier ^3.5.3, ESLint ^9.28, typescript-eslint ^8.33. Note: default auth mode changed from 'read-only' to 'open' for development ergonomics.\"\n227\t  - session: 22\n228\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n229\t    summary: \"User asked to update subordinate expertise files (library-developer and library-validator had stale expertise after Phase 2/3 completion and Biome→ESLint+Prettier swap). Delegated expertise updates to both agents in parallel. Both completed successfully: library-developer updated with full Phase 2/3 details, tooling swap, CLI commands, architecture, type system, testing patterns. library-validator updated with deprecated Biome learnings, current coverage (99.22%/100%), full source/test layout, ESLint/Prettier patterns. Both verified quality gates pass before finalizing. No code changes — expertise maintenance only.\"\n230\t  - session: 23\n231\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n232\t    summary: \"User requested Phase 4 implementation. Created detailed Phase 4 spec (07-phase4-comments-spec.md) covering computeComments, 4 Tracker methods, CLI commands, test plan. Delegated to library-developer — completed in single delegation (193 tests, 926 assertions). Verified quality gates independently. Delegated to library-validator for validation — found and filled auth integration gaps, added 23 more tests. Final: 216 tests, 972 assertions, 99.22% coverage. Updated status.yaml and cto-index.yaml with post-validation numbers. Phase 4 complete.\"\n233\t  - session: 24\n234\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n235\t    summary: \"User noticed library-developer expertise was stale after Phase 4. Delegated expertise update to library-developer. No code changes — expertise maintenance only.\"\n236\t  - session: 25\n237\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n238\t    summary: \"User requested Phase 5 implementation. Created detailed Phase 5 spec (08-phase5-hierarchy-spec.md) covering childrenOf map management, hierarchy constraint module (validateNewChild, validateParentStatusChange, getClosableChildren, computeUpwardPromotions), Tracker create/update integration with downward cascade + upward auto-promotion + reparenting, HIERARCHY_CONSTRAINT error code. Delegated to library-developer — task running in background. No CLI changes needed (--parentId already supported from Phase 2).\"\n239\t  - session: 26\n240\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n241\t    summary: \"Phase 5 complete. library-developer implemented: hierarchy.ts (5 pure constraint functions), childrenOf management in index-manager.ts, Tracker create/update integration with downward cascade + upward auto-promotion + reparenting. 56 new tests. library-validator validated: added 12 more tests (auth integration, edge cases, CLI hierarchy). Final: 284 tests, 1101 assertions, 99.31% coverage. All quality gates pass. Updated expertise and status. Ready for Phase 6 (blockages). Also updated delegation workflow: quality agent should always receive the same spec as the developer.\"\n242\t  - session: 27\n243\t    date: \"2026-05-10\"\n244\t    summary: \"Phase 6 implementation. Created Phase 6 spec (07-phase6-blockages-spec.md) with full details: dependency-manager (7 functions including cycle detection via transitive blockedBy walk, batch atomicity with projected state), 4 Tracker methods, auto-resolution on done/closed status transitions, impact score in list sort, CLI blockages commands. Delegated to library-developer — completed. Files modified: dependency-manager.ts (full implementation), tracker.ts (blockage methods + auto-resolution + impact sort), events.ts, runner.ts, blockages.ts (new CLI commands). New tests: dependency-manager.test.ts. library-validator validation delegated and running in background.\"\n245\t  - session: 28\n246\t    date: \"2026-05-11\"\n247\t    summary: \"library-validator refactored large test files into smaller per-feature files. Ran refactored tracker.test.ts: 163 tests, 429 assertions, 100% lines, all green. Delegated expertise update to library-validator to document new test structure. library-validator updated: 528 tests, 1793 assertions total. New layout: tests/core/tracker/ (8 split files), tests/core/events/ (4 split files), naming convention {module}-{feature}.test.ts, split threshold ~500 lines. Monolithic files marked deprecated.\"\n248\t  - session: 29\n249\t    date: \"2026-05-11\"\n250\t    summary: \"Stop hook triggered expertise update. Reviewed current state: Phase 7 spec (08-phase7-polish-spec.md) exists as untracked file. Uncommitted code changes in hierarchy.ts (4 changes), tracker.ts (50 changes), hierarchy.test.ts (10 changes) — likely Phase 7 work in progress. Updated expertise files to reflect Phase 7 status and new spec.\"\n251\t  - session: 30\n252\t    date: \"2026-05-11\"\n253\t    summary: \"Phase 7 implementation complete. Delegated all 4 tasks to library-developer: (1) Error message polish — IDs wrapped in backticks, consistent format, (2) JSDoc on all public exports — Tracker class + 17 methods, all type files, errors, (3) Edge case testing — 18 new tests (empty tracker, corrupt JSON, missing files, 100+ events, self-blockage, no-op updates), (4) Package config — prepublishOnly script, 3 new tests (package.json fields, CLI --help, --version). Final: 549 tests, 1948 assertions, all quality gates pass. Updated status.yaml and cto-index.yaml. All 7 implementation phases now complete.\"\n254\t  - session: 31\n255\t    date: \"2026-05-11\"\n256\t    summary: \"Delegated expertise update to library-developer for Phase 7 changes. Discussed next steps with user: (1) commit Phase 7 changes, (2) library-validator validation for Phase 7 (skipped earlier but mandatory workflow says developer→quality), (3) build/npm distribution strategy — current package.json points to raw .ts files which works for Bun but not Node.js, needs build step or Bun-only scoping, (4) resolve open questions OQ-003 (concurrent writes) and OQ-004 (CLAUDE.md), (5) generate API docs via TypeDoc. Recommended order: commit → library-validator review → build strategy decision. Awaiting user direction.\"\n257\t  - session: 32\n258\t    date: \"2026-05-11\"\n259\t    summary: \"User asked for build and documentation tooling recommendations. Reviewed current project setup (package.json, tsconfig, typedoc.json, source structure). Made two key decisions: (1) Build: tsup — purpose-built for TS→npm library builds, generates ESM + CJS + .d.ts + CLI binary bundle, replaces raw TS source shipping. (2) Docs: TypeDoc HTML — already installed and parsing cleanly with JSDoc on all exports, just switch from typedoc-plugin-markdown to default HTML output for publishable docs. Key prerequisites: verify Node.js compat in file-io.ts (replace Bun.file/Bun.write with node:fs if needed), update shebang from bun to node, update package.json exports. Awaiting user go-ahead to write formal spec and delegate implementation.\"\n260\t  - session: 33\n261\t    date: \"2026-05-11\"\n262\t    summary: \"User approved. Created Phase 8 build spec (.agentic/specs/09-phase8-build-spec.md). Delegated to library-developer — completed successfully. Key finding: no Bun-specific APIs existed in the codebase (already using node:fs/promises). tsup.config.ts created with dual entry points (library ESM+CJS+dts, CLI binary bundled). package.json updated for dist/-based distribution with node>=20 engine. Delegated to library-validator for validation — all gates pass: 549 tests, 1950 assertions, typecheck clean, lint clean. CJS+ESM imports verified. CLI binary verified end-to-end (init, create, list, view). Build pipeline fully operational.\"\n263\t  - session: 34\n264\t    date: \"2026-05-11\"\n265\t    summary: \"Designed publish pipeline for npm + GitHub Pages docs. Two GitHub Actions workflows: (1) CI — quality gates on every push/PR to main, (2) Release — triggered by version tag push (v*), runs quality → build → npm publish → TypeDoc HTML → deploy to GitHub Pages. Single sequential job in release ensures docs don't deploy if npm publish fails. Developer workflow: npm version patch → git push --follow-tags. One-time manual setup: NPM_TOKEN secret, GitHub Pages source set to 'GitHub Actions'. TypeDoc output to docs-html/ directory. Awaiting user approval to create formal spec and delegate implementation.\"\n266\t  - session: 35\n267\t    date: \"2026-05-11\"\n268\t    summary: \"User clarified library-validator owns documentation tasks (not library-developer). Created spec 10-publish-pipeline-spec.md. Delegated to library-validator: TypeDoc HTML config done (typedoc.json updated, docs script added, docs-html/ generated with full API docs). CI/Release workflows and .gitignore update blocked — no agent has write access to .github/ or root .gitignore. Access boundary gap identified: .github/workflows/ falls outside all three agents' access rules. User needs to create .github/workflows/{ci,release}.yml and append docs-html/ to .gitignore manually. Also learned: typedoc-plugin-markdown is now unused but still in devDependencies — cleanup opportunity.\"\n269\t  - session: 36\n270\t    date: \"2026-05-11\"\n271\t    summary: \"User granted CTO access to .github/ folder. Created CI workflow (.github/workflows/ci.yml) and Release workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml). Updated .gitignore with docs-html/ entry. Publish pipeline now fully implemented. Remaining manual steps for user: add NPM_TOKEN secret, set GitHub Pages source to 'GitHub Actions', cut first v0.1.0 tag.\"\n272\t  - session: 37\n273\t    date: \"2026-05-12\"\n274\t    summary: \"Created README.md at project root: introduction, install, quick start (CLI + programmatic API), how it works (file structure, event sourcing), status flow, hierarchy constraints, auth configuration, license link. Created LICENSE file (MIT, 2026).\"\n275\t  - session: 38\n276\t    date: \"2026-05-12\"\n277\t    summary: \"Started dogfooding — agentrack now tracks its own development. Linked CLI globally via `npm link` from packages/library/ (symlinks agt → packages/library/dist/bin.js). Initialized .agentrack/ at repo root (NOT inside packages/library/ — that was accidental first run, user cleaned it up). Created test issue mp27msuvaj ('Test: verify dogfooding setup works'). Workflow: rebuild with `bun run build` in packages/library/, then `agt` picks up fresh build via symlink. Issues committed to git via .agentrack/ at repo root.\"\n278\t  - session: 39\n279\t    date: \"2026-05-13\"\n280\t    summary: \"Organized all pending work from status.yaml into agentrack issues. Closed test issue mp27msuvaj (dogfooding confirmed working). Created 7 issues: mp3pe95w9e (P1, defensive index validation), mp3pe9lvdq (P2, typedoc-plugin-markdown cleanup), mp3peanz8b (P2, v0.1.0 release milestone), mp3peac1qo (P2, NPM_TOKEN config — child of release), mp3peawcgs (P2, GitHub Pages config — child of release), mp3pe96e9f (P3, concurrent file access decision), mp3pe9urb9 (P4, CLAUDE.md decision). agentrack is now the single source of truth for all pending work.\"\n281\t  - session: 40\n282\t    date: \"2026-05-13\"\n283\t    summary: \"User requested `next <user-name>` subcommand. Designed spec (.agentic/specs/next-command-spec.md): returns single best issue to work on for a given user. Filters open index to assignee match + actionable statuses (idea/todo/in-progress), excludes actively blocked issues, sorts by priority ASC → impact DESC → id ASC, returns full ComputedIssue or NO_ISSUES_AVAILABLE. Delegated to library-developer — implemented in 6 files (NextResult type, Tracker.next() method, CLI command handler, runner registration, type exports). Delegated to library-validator — validated spec compliance, added 20 tests (14 unit + 6 CLI). Final: 569 tests, 1997 assertions, 100% tracker.ts line coverage. Issue mp3rc7femf.\"\n284\t  - session: 41\n285\t    date: \"2026-05-13\"\n286\t    summary: \"Updated README.md with `next` command in both CLI quick start and programmatic API sections. No code changes — documentation only.\"\n287\t  - session: 42\n288\t    date: \"2026-05-14\"\n289\t    summary: \"First `/worktask` invocation via the new agent runner mechanism (issue mp5r0cd19j — test task to verify runner works). Received issue via worktask skill, followed full workflow: viewed issue, validated assignment/blockages/status, handled `idea` status correctly (commented with analysis rather than making code changes). Runner mechanism confirmed working.\"\n290\t  - session: 43\n291\t    date: \"2026-05-14\"\n292\t    summary: \"Third `/worktask` invocation for mp5r0cd19j. Issue was still in `idea` status despite two previous analysis comments. Added third analysis comment noting prior invocations and recommending move to `todo` for completion. Updated expertise files — refined expertise_status with agent runner testing details.\"\n293\t  - session: 44\n294\t    date: \"2026-05-17\"\n295\t    summary: \"User requested `next` command change: restrict to `todo` status only (currently accepts idea/todo/in-progress). Drafted spec (.agentic/specs/next-todo-only-spec.md). Created issue chain: parent mp9kuwi7dt (blocked by dev review mp9kv3umii + quality review mp9kv3wyao). Awaiting review feedback before finalizing spec and creating implementation tasks.\"\n296\t  - session: 45\n297\t    date: \"2026-05-17\"\n298\t    summary: \"User requested change to auto-promotion mechanism: parents should NOT auto-promote to done when all children finish. Drafted spec (.agentic/specs/cap-upward-promotion-spec.md). Created issue chain: parent mp9xefucmo (in-progress), reviews mp9xemq9mv (dev) + mp9xemy1j3 (quality), implement mp9xevrbwj (blocked by reviews), validate mp9xev4b6c (blocked by implementation). Key insight: computeUpwardPromotions in hierarchy.ts walks parent chain promoting to child's status — needs to cap promoted status at in-progress.\"\n299\t  - session: 46\n300\t    date: \"2026-05