ibrary-validator and library-releaser focus areas. No code changes.\"\n311\t  - session: 50\n312\t    date: \"2026-05-17\"\n313\t    summary: \"Revisited mpa5yz3kei via /agentrack-implement. Previous session had already completed CTO expertise update and library-validator child task. Accidentally created duplicate child issues (mpa63iwwhf, mpa63qxqpr — closed them). Verified remaining blocker: mpa60i4skg (library-releaser expertise init, todo, awaiting agent runner). Parent stays in-progress until library-releaser completes onboarding. No expertise changes needed — already accurate.\"\n314\t  - session: 51\n315\t    date: \"2026-05-18\"\n316\t    summary: \"User reported `agt` not available on command line after rename from trackgentic to agentrack. Diagnosed: package.json correctly has bin.agt → dist/bin.js and dist exists, but global npm link was stale/broken after rename. Fix: re-run `npm link` from packages/library/. Updated expertise: expertise_status and project_overview updated with rename context, status.yaml dogfooding notes updated with rename_note and symlink warning.\"\n317\t  - session: 52\n318\t    date: \"2026-05-19\"\n319\t    summary: \"Reviewed and evolved independent-git.md spec. Three rounds of corrections: (1) Naming conventions: branch = `_agentrack`, directory = `.agentrack`, tool = `agentrack`, data inside branch = `issues/`. (2) Directory structure: replaced fake layout with real `.agentrack/` contents (config.json, index.json, dependencies.json, users.json, issues/*.json). (3) Added two init scenarios: Scenario A (fresh setup — no remote branch, create orphan) and Scenario B (join existing — remote branch exists, fetch + track + mount). Decision logic: `git ls-remote --heads origin _agentrack`.\"\n320\t  - session: 53\n321\t    date: \"2026-05-19\"\n322\t    summary: \"Planned documentation generation feature. Created spec (.agentic/specs/docs-generation.md) for dual-format docs: HTML (docs/html/) for users + Markdown (docs/md/) for agents.