ent: cto\n# Domain: Project architecture, technical specifications, development alignment\n\nhierarchy:\n  manager: none — top-level agent\n  subordinates:\n    active:\n      - library-developer (implementation)\n      - library-validator (testing, quality gates — documentation removed)\n      - library-releaser (release prep, documentation, build, version management, publishing)\n      - webapp-developer (full-stack web development — React frontend + Hono backend)\n      - webapp-validator (webapp testing, quality assurance, spec compliance)\n      - webapp-styler (UI/UX expert — visual design, interaction patterns, accessibility, polish)\n    pending_setup: []\n\nexpertise_status: \"Webapp initiative (parent mppqqp8y26, in-progress). Phases 1-3 done. Phase 4 impl (mppqswn3jl) in-progress with webapp-developer. Phase 4 validation (mppqt90kot) todo, blocked by mppqswn3jl. E2E isolation FIXED: mpr50trdgw + mpr51myb9q both DONE. Delete command FULLY COMPLETE: impl (mps4sfny0f) done, validation (mps4uwcsqx) done, bug fix (mpscu5l9rk+mpscw71ria) done, docs (mps4viae0a) done — both cli-reference.md and javascript-reference.md updated. Board: 13 issues (10 done, 2 in-progress, 1 todo). webapp-styler active but no assigned issues.\"\n\nproject_overview:\n  name: agentrack\n  previous_name: trackgentic (renamed 2026-05-18)\n  type: npm library (TypeScript, Bun runtime)\n  purpose: Issue tracker designed for AI agents — file-backed, event-sourced, git-friendly\n  distribution: npm package with CLI entry point (`agt` command)\n  stage: \"Dogfooding active. All 7 library phases complete + build pipeline. Delete command shipped. Mentions feature shipped. Webapp initiative active (parent mppqqp8y26, in-progress): Phases 1-3 done, Phase 4 (users & sync) in-progress with webapp-developer (mppqswn3jl). E2E isolation fixed (dedicated test ports). Public docs at docs/markdown/ (8 files).\"\n  bun_version: \"1.3.11\"\n  build_tool: tsup (implemented, producing dist/)\n  docs_tool: \"Hand-written markdown docs in docs/markdown/ (8 sections). TypeDoc removed. Docs overhaul in progress (mpdpt4rego), validation pending (mpdpv6gw49). Future: Docusaurus site consuming docs/markdown/ (mpdxdbqwt9, idea). Spec: .agentic/specs/user-docs-spec.md.\"\n\ndetail_files:\n  - path: architecture.yaml\n    description: Core data model, file structure, event sourcing, resolution algorithm, index design\n  - path: design-decisions.yaml\n    description: Architectural decisions and rationale (why file-backed, why event-sourced, etc.)\n  - path: status.yaml\n    description: Current project status, implementation roadmap, open questions, risks\n\nspecifications:\n  location: .agentic/specs/\n  files:\n    - path: 01-overview.md\n      description: Monorepo structure, library package layout, design principles, dependencies, CLI/API relationship\n    - path: 02-data-model.md\n      description: All TypeScript types, interfaces, file formats, initial file contents\n    - path: 03-api-specification.md\n      description: Every Tracker method with params, return types, behavior, error handling\n    - path: 04-cli-specification.md\n      description: Every CLI command with args, flags, auth, output format, error handling\n    - path: 05-implementation-phases.md\n      description: 7 phases from foundation to polish, with tasks, tests, and exit criteria per phase\n    - path: 06-quality-plan.md\n      description: Quality plan — now uses Prettier + ESLint (was Biome). Linting, typechecking (strict+), testing (Bun), test organization, documentation (TypeDoc), quality gates\n    - path: 07-phase3-auth-users.md\n      description: Phase 3 specification — auth module (resolveAuthor), user CRUD (register/list/revoke/regenerate), auth integration into existing methods, CLI user commands\n    - path: 07-phase4-comments-spec.md\n      description: Phase 4 specification — computeComments function, 4 Tracker comment methods, CLI comment commands, test plan\n    - path: 08-phase5-hierarchy-spec.md\n      description: Phase 5 specification — childrenOf map management, hierarchy.ts (upward/downward constraints), Tracker create/update integration, reparenting, test plan\n    - path: 07-phase6-blockages-spec.md\n      description: Phase 6 specification — dependency-manager (bidirectional maps, cycle detection, batch atomicity, impact score), 4 Tracker blockage methods, auto-resolution on status change, CLI blockage commands, test plan\n    - path: 08-phase7-polish-spec.md\n      description: Phase 7 specification — JSDoc on all public API, error message polish, edge case & resilience testing, package configuration verification\n    - path: next-command-spec.md\n      description: \"`next <user-name>` command — recommend highest-priority unblocked issue for a user. Returns ComputedIssue or NO_ISSUES_AVAILABLE. Filters by assignee, actionable statuses (idea/todo/in-progress), no active blockages. Sort: priority ASC → impact DESC → id ASC.\"\n    - path: next-todo-only-spec.md\n      description: \"Amends next-command-spec: restrict status filter from [idea, todo, in-progress] to [todo] only. Single-line change in Tracker.next(). REVIEWED — reviews skipped (trivially scoped). Implementation mp9zda04cp in-progress with library-developer.\"\n    - path: cap-upward-promotion-spec.md\n      description: \"Cap upward auto-promotion at in-progress. Parents never auto-promote to done/closed via computeUpwardPromotions. Spec status: REVIEWED. Reason format: auto-promoted to TARGET: child advanced to CHILD. 7 new test cases required.\"\n    - path: independent-git-spec.md\n      description: \"Store .agentrack/ on orphan branch _agentrack via git worktree. Branch-independent issue access. Two init scenarios (fresh/join). Three commands: agt init (worktree setup), agt push (auto-commit + sync), agt pull (sync from remote). New module src/worktree.ts + 2 new CLI commands. Status: IMPLEMENTED with 3 spec deviations found in validation. Fix phase: mpd4hktoxq (fix deviations) → mpd4hs14zp (validate + tests) → mpd4i06wz6 (document + build). Parent: mpcwcufhzk.\"\n      naming_conventions: \"Branch = `_agentrack`, directory = `.agentrack`, tool = `agentrack`, data inside branch = `issues/`\"\n    - path: docs-generation.md\n      description: \"SUPERSEDED by user-docs-spec.md. TypeDoc dual-format docs are being removed. Release workflow and .gitignore updated by CTO (mpdpvfn3yb done). Typedoc tooling cleanup pending (mpdpu00ksc).\"\n    - path: user-docs-spec.md\n      description: \"User-friendly documentation overhaul. Replace TypeDoc auto-generated docs with hand-written markdown in docs/markdown/. 8 sections: overview, getting started, authentication, issue object, hierarchy & blockages, storing in git, CLI reference, JS reference. Removes typedoc tooling entirely. Parent: mpdpt4rego. CTO config (mpdpvfn3yb) done. TypeDoc deps removed from package.json. Doc writing: mpdwq7dvls (library-releaser, replaces failed mpdpuhd0r5).\"\n    - path: configurable-branch-spec.md\n      description: \"Configurable branch name for agt init. --branch <name> flag allows custom orphan branch per agentrack instance. Normalization: strip leading _, prepend _ for branch, . for dir. Pointer file (.agentrack.json) at repo root solves circular discovery. Slash rejection (AC8). resolution.ts and tracker.ts dynamic discovery via pointer file. New module: src/core/pointer.ts (actually implemented as branch-config.ts). Enables multiple instances per repo and test isolation. IMPLEMENTED (mpfm9aff8v) but validation (mpfm9ixr9i) found 2 critical bugs: (1) double directory creation — tracker init runs before branch flag takes effect, leaving stale .agentrack/ alongside custom dir, (2) missing BRANCH_CONFLICT detection. Fix: mpfn4dkotn (library-developer). Parent: mpfm8bilwf. Spec status: REVIEWED.\"\n    - path: e2e-validation-suite-spec.md\n      description: \"E2E test suite in validation/ folder. Uses real git repos + agt CLI invocations (spawn + capture). Covers all CLI commands with happy/error/edge cases. Full lifecycle test. No library code changes. Parent: mpebmstgs9. Implementation: mpebnnq5qq (library-validator).\"\n    - path: e2e-refactor.md\n      description: \"Refactor E2E tests from per-test git repos to shared worktree approach. Two test types: Type A (git ops: init/push/pull, clean git env per test) and Type B (CRUD etc., fast data reset per test). New helpers: initE2EWorktree, teardownE2EWorktree, resetWorktreeData, setAuthMode. Remove old helpers: createTestRepo, cleanupTestRepo, createIsolatedDir. Parent: mpfobnq8ty (child of mpebmstgs9). Implementation: mpfobxibgb (library-validator). Validation: mpfoc9r65a (library-validator).\"\n    - path: webapp-spec.md\n      description: \"Full-stack webapp specification for agentrack UI. React 19 + Vite + shadcn/ui frontend (SPA with list and detail views), Hono + Bun backend (REST API with 21 endpoints), TanStack Query state management. Covers API design (issues, comments, blockages, users, sync, health), UI/UX design (tree view, filters, inline editing, responsive layout), project structure, color scheme. v1 scope excludes init, custom branches, auth UI, real-time, markdown rendering, dark mode.\"\n    - path: webapp-roadmap.md\n      description: \"5-phase development roadmap for the webapp. Phase 1: Foundation (scaffolding, health check). Phase 2: Core issues (CRUD endpoints, list page, detail page, create dialog). Phase 3: Rich detail (comments, blockages, history, tree view, tags, parent). Phase 4: Users & sync (user management UI, push/pull controls). Phase 5: Polish (responsive, loading states, sorting, filtering). 10 implementation issues with blocking dependencies.\"\n    - path: webapp-agent-setup.md\n      description: \"Setup guide for webapp-developer and webapp-validator agents. Contains full agent configurations (frontmatter + system prompts) and expertise index templates. Agents registered in agentrack but need manual file creation in .claude/agents/ and .agentic/expertise/.\"\n    - path: delete-command-spec.md\n      description: \"Spec for agt delete <issue-id> command. Hard delete of issue and all descendants. Cleans blockages (bidirectional), mentions, parent-child relationships, and event file from disk. Returns deletedIds array (children first, target last). New types: IssueDeleteParams, IssueDeleteResult. New helpers: removeIssueMentions, removeAllBlockagesForIssue. Parent: mps4sfny0f.\"\n\naccess_boundaries:\n  rule: \"CTO must NOT read or modify files under packages/library/. All code changes go through subordinates.\"\n  cto_scope: \".agentic/ files, root-level config, specifications, expertise files\"\n  code_access: \"If code-level insight is needed, ask library-developer or library-validator to report — never read source directly.\"\n  enforced: \"2026-05-10 — user explicitly removed CTO read permissions on packages/library/\"\n\ndelegation_workflow:\n  mandatory_sequence: |\n    After every library-developer delegation that makes code changes, you MUST delegate to library-validator for validation.\n    Sequence: library-developer (implement) → library-validator (validate).\n    Never skip the quality validation step. This ensures code is clean, tested, and documented.\n  timeout_constraint: |\n    Bash tool has a 10-minute (600000ms) timeout. Large phases must be split into sub-delegations of ~5-8 minutes each.\n    Split strategy for Phase 3: (A) auth.ts + errors.ts, (B) user methods in tracker.ts, (C) auth integration into existing methods + CLI commands, (D) library-validator validation).\n    Each sub-task should be scoped to a few files to stay within timeout.\n  docs_ownership: |\n    library-releaser owns documentation tasks: TypeDoc configuration, doc generation, docs scripts.\n    When docs need updating or generating for a release, delegate to library-releaser.\n    library-validator no longer handles documentation — only testing and quality gates.\n  api_change_policy: |\n 