tion_pattern: |\n    Webapp issues follow sequential phases: impl → validate → next phase impl.\n    ALL issues in a chain should be set to todo upfront. Blockages control the execution order.\n    Only todo issues are picked up by `agt next`. Idea is invisible to the runner.\n    Do NOT use idea status for work that should flow through the agent runner automatically.\n  webapp_styler_pattern: |\n    webapp-styler is a UI/UX specialist — does NOT write backend code or tests.\n    Workflow: (1) webapp-styler audits UI and posts findings comment, (2) CTO reviews findings\n    and creates implementation issues, (3) webapp-styler implements changes within scope.\n    webapp-styler's domain: CSS, component styling, layout, accessibility, responsive design,\n    interaction patterns, visual consistency, micro-interactions.\n    webapp-styler does NOT own: backend API, data model, business logic, test infrastructure.\n    Currently no assigned issues — cleared in session 87. Ready for new tasks when needed.\n  note: \"Self-check and validation steps are enforced via agent system prompts. No need to duplicate in delegation messages.\"\n  library-developer:\n    focus: \"Focus delegation messages on the implementation task itself. The agent self-checks typecheck+lint+test before completion.\"\n  library-validator:\n    focus: \"Always pass the same spec file used for implementation so quality can validate alignment with specs, not just code quality. Include the spec path, what changed, and what behaviors to validate. Handles testing and quality gates only (documentation moved to library-releaser).\"\n  library-releaser:\n    focus: \"Delegate release tasks: verify quality gates pass, generate documentation (HTML + Markdown), build artifacts, bump version, publish to npm. Provide version bump guidance (patch/minor/major) based on changes since last release. The agent owns the full release lifecycle end-to-end. Docs output: docs/html/ (users) + docs/md/ (agents) at repo root. 