se.yml (npm publish + docs deploy on v* tag)\n      gitignore_update: complete — docs-html/ added\n    remaining:\n      - \"All tracked as agentrack issues — see `agt list` for current backlog\"\n      - \"Webapp initiative: ACTIVE (parent mppqqp8y26, in-progress). Phases 1-3 done. Phase 4 impl in-progress. E2E isolation done. UI/UX audit ready for webapp-styler.\"\n      - \"Webapp specs: .agentic/specs/webapp-spec.md (API + UI design) + webapp-roadmap.md (5-phase plan)\"\n      - \"Webapp agents: webapp-developer + webapp-validator + webapp-styler fully set up\"\n      - \"Delete command: NEW (parent mps4sfny0f, todo). agt delete <issue-id> with cascade. Spec at .agentic/specs/delete-command-spec.md\"\n      - \"Old issues (configurable branch, E2E tests, docs overhaul) from previous worktree branch — not in current index\"\n      - \"POLICY: any CLI/API change must route to library-releaser for build + docs update\"\n      - \"DOCS: all agents have read access to docs/markdown/ — mention in task descriptions when relevant\"\n\nimplementation_roadmap:\n  source: .agentic/specs/05-implementation-phases.md\n  phases:\n    phase_1_foundation:\n      description: \"Project setup, types, ID generation, directory resolution, file I/O, init command, CLI runner\"\n      exit_criteria: \"agt init creates .agentrack/ with correct files, idempotent on re-run\"\n      status: complete\n    phase_2_event_engine_and_crud:\n      description: \"Event append/replay engine, index manager with binary search, create/update/list/view/history\"\n      exit_criteria: \"Full CRUD cycle works: create → list → view → update → view → history\"\n      status: complete\n    phase_3_auth_and_users:\n      description: \"Auth module (token resolution, mode enforcement), user CRUD (register/list/revoke/regenerate)\"\n      exit_criteria: \"Token-based auth enforced per mode, author in all events\"\n      status: complete\n      notes: \"Default auth mode changed to 'open' for dev ergonomics. Tooling swapped from Biome to Prettier + ESLint.\"\n    phase_4_comments:\n      description: \"Comment lifecycle: add/update/delete/list with event replay\"\n      exit_criteria: \"Full comment CRUD with computed state from event replay\"\n      status: complete\n      notes: \"26 new tests. computeComments function added to events.ts. 4 Tracker methods + CLI commands.\"\n    phase_5_hierarchy:\n      description: \"childrenOf map, upward auto-promotion, downward cascade, reparenting\"\n      exit_criteria: \"Tree constraints enforced, system-authored events in history\"\n      status: complete\n      notes: \"68 new tests (56 developer + 12 quality). hierarchy.ts pure function module. Recursive upward promotion + downward cascade.\"\n    phase_6_blockages:\n      description: \"Dependency maps, cycle detection, batch atomicity, auto-resolution, impact score\"\n      exit_criteria: \"Full blockage lifecycle with cycle detection and auto-resolution\"\n      status: complete\n      notes: \"dependency-manager.ts fully implemented. 4 Tracker methods + auto-resolution + impact score + CLI commands. Quality validated.\"\n    phase_7_polish:\n      description: \"Edge case testing, package config, error messages, JSDoc\"\n      exit_criteria: \"Package installs and CLI works from any directory, all tests pass\"\n      status: complete\n      notes: \"All 4 tasks done. JSDoc on all public exports. Error messages polished (backtick IDs, consistent format). 21 new tests (18 edge cases + 3 package config). prepublishOnly script added. 549 total tests, 1948 assertions.\"\n  phase_7_results:\n    tests: 569 passing, 1997 assertions\n    typecheck: clean (strict + 4 extra flags)\n    lint: clean (ESLint, zero errors)\n    format: clean (Prettier, zero issues)\n    docs_check: clean (TypeDoc parses all source)\n    new_files:\n      tests: tests/integration/edge-cases.test.ts (18 tests), tests/integration/package.test.ts (3 tests)\n    modified_files:\n      core: tracker.ts (JSDoc on class + all 17 methods, error messages with backtick IDs), hierarchy.ts (error messages polished), errors.ts (JSDoc)\n      types: issue.ts, event.ts, index-file.ts, dependency.ts, user.ts, config.ts, api.ts (all JSDoc)\n      tests: hierarchy.test.ts, tracker.test.ts, tracker-hierarchy.test.ts (error message assertion updates)\n      config: package.json (added prepublishOnly script)\n    design_decisions:\n      - Error messages consistently wrap IDs in backticks for readability\n      - Error messages always end with period\n      - JSDoc uses @param, @returns, @throws, @example tags\n      - Edge case tests document concurrent write limitation as a known constraint\n      - CLI --version returns package.json version (0.1.0)\n\nopen_questions:\n  - id: OQ-001\n    question: \"Where should technical specs be written?\"\n    answer: \".agentic/specs/ — chosen for proximity to agent config\"\n    status: resolved\n    resolved_date: \"2026-05-10\"\n\n  - id: OQ-002\n    question: \"Should we have a programmatic API in addition to CLI?\"\n    answer: \"Yes — Tracker class is the core API. CLI is a thin wrapper. Both return identical JSON structures.\"\n    status: resolved\n    resolved_date: \"2026-05-10\"\n\n  - id: OQ-003\n    question: \"Should the library handle concurrent file access?\"\n    context: \"Multiple agents writing to same files simultaneously\"\n    status: unresolved\n    notes: \"File-level locking? Atomic writes? May not be needed for MVP\"\n\n  - id: OQ-004\n    question: \"Should we add a CLAUDE.md at project root?\"\n    context: \"claude-developer noted this as an open question\"\n    status: unresolved\n    notes: \"Useful for onboarding but not blocking implementation\"\n\nrisks:\n  - id: RSK-001\n    risk: \"File corruption from concurrent agent writes\"\n    severity: medium\n    mitigation: \"Atomic write patterns (write to temp, rename). May add file locking later.\"\n    status: acknowledged\n\n  - id: RSK-002\n    risk: \"Index getting out of sync with issue files\"\n    severity: high\n    mitigation: \"Index updates must be atomic with issue file writes. Defensive reads should validate.\"\n    status: acknowledged\n\n  - id: RSK-003\n    risk: \"Status cascade performance with deep hierarchies\"\n    severity: low\n    mitigation: \"Agent trackers unlikely to have deep trees. Can optimize later if needed.\"\n    status: acknowledged\n\n  - id: RSK-004\n    risk: \"Cycle detection performance with many blockages\"\n    severity: low\n    mitigation: \"Only active entries checked. Agent-scale graphs are small.\"\n    status: acknowledged\n\narchitectural_notes:\n  - \"The two-event creation pattern (creation event + update event with initial properties) is intentional — it simplifies state reconstruction since update events always carry the full property changes\"\n  - \"The 'system' author for auto-promotion events is distinct from user-authored events — this is important for audit trails\"\n  - \"Comment IDs need a generation strategy — docs don't specify the format, but should follow a similar pattern to issue IDs\"\n  - \"The batch blockage operations (multiple --by args) need careful ordering for cycle detection against projected state\"\n","numLines":455,"startLine":1,"totalLines":455}},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"553db555-519a-48ec-a18a-8745161ef5a8","userType":"external","entrypoint":"sdk-cli","cwd":"/Users/javi/projects/agentrack","sessionId":"27152081-2b2a-4a32-8c49-5eb5356fd1c4","version":"2.1.159","gitBranch":"main"}
